course: dictionary
lesson: 1538
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Chad is one of them: it can be a country, a man's name, a tiny bit of paper, or a joke name online. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «People in Japan live into their mid-80s on average, while in Chad and some other poor countries life expectancy is in the 50s.» Japan is a country, and life expectancy is about how long people live, so Chad must be a country too.
explain: Then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Calling someone a Chad» is about a person, not a place, so here Chad is a slang word for a joke name. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the words around it?
fact: Chad is a large country in north-central Africa, and its capital is N'Djamena.
fact: Chad is also a man's name, like Sam or Jack.
fact: A chad is the tiny bit of paper punched out when you make a hole in a card or ballot paper.
fact: In slang, «a Chad» is a joke name for a confident, sporty, popular young man, and it can be used to tease people.
fact: Check the clues first: a place, a person, a piece of paper, or a joke. The words around the word tell you which one it is.
exercise: «The UN reported that more than 12 million people in Sudan were forced from their homes, many fleeing to neighbouring countries such as Chad and Egypt.» What is Chad in this sentence? | A man's name | A tiny bit of paper | *A country | A joke name for a popular young man
exercise: Ben says, «Chad is my friend's name.» What is Chad in this sentence? | A country in Africa | A word that means very old | *A man's name | A bit of paper punched out of a card
exercise: «Hanging chads on old paper ballots caused arguments about counting votes.» What is a chad here? | A joke name for a sporty young man | *A tiny bit of paper punched out of a card | A country in north-central Africa
test: «In geography, we learned that Chad has no coast, so it is landlocked.» What is Chad in this sentence? | *A country | A bit of paper | A lake | A joke name
test: «Some people think calling someone a Chad is funny, but it can be teasing and mean.» What does a Chad mean here? | A man's name, like Sam | *A joke name for a confident, sporty, popular young man | A country in Africa | A tiny bit of paper punched out of a card
exam: «The herds of oryx now have calves in the wild, and they were released in Chad.» Which meaning of Chad fits here? | A man's name | *A country in north-central Africa | A joke name for a popular young man | A bit of paper punched out of a card
